From da542db44de1459494bdd082c2b5f78d3339495d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 22:04:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] version: bump EXTENDNO to Reaper_v2.4.1

v2.4.0 images are already on the release ladder and were flashed for field
testing; the tree has moved six commits past that point (Phase 2/3 firewall,
the mesh firmware page, the two v2.3.9 metal fixes, the opaque-header fix, the
measured engine-active signal and backup box, the devices export and the
dashboard posture links). Reusing 2.4.0 would put two different images behind
one version string, which is exactly what makes a field report unusable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src-rt/version.conf | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src-rt/version.conf b/release/src-rt/version.conf
index 9b69265d5d..70417f5c85 100644
--- a/release/src-rt/version.conf
+++ b/release/src-rt/version.conf
@@ -4,6 +4,6 @@ KERNEL_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(KERNEL_VER))
 FS_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(FS_VER))
 
 SERIALNO=102.8
-EXTENDNO=Reaper_v2.4.0
+EXTENDNO=Reaper_v2.4.1
 
 RCNO=0
-- 
2.25.1

